    dc:type "resolution-route/mixed";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: For explicitly sampled simple-program families, search for algebraic invariants, compression, prediction shortcuts, and universality proofs beyond repetition and nesting. Discovery of a broad exploitable invariant would refute a restricted version; repeated failure would not prove absence.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "A 'large class' and 'hidden regularity' have no unique definitions.", "Absence of hidden regularity is not finitely verifiable.", "Universality does not imply absence of all useful regularities.";
